course: dictionary
lesson: 7597
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it. Those words are its context, and they give you clues. «In the UK you do not vote for the prime minister directly.» Here prime minister is a job title: the person who leads the government.
explain: Prime can also mean main or most important, or of the best quality. In «a prime example», it means the very best example of something. Try your meaning in the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have probably found the right one.
explain: In maths, a prime number is a whole number greater than 1 that can only be divided exactly by 1 and itself. 7 is prime, because only 1 and 7 divide it exactly. 8 is not prime, because 2 and 4 also divide it exactly.
fact: Prime means main or most important, as in «a prime example».
fact: A prime number is a whole number greater than 1 that only divides exactly by 1 and itself.
fact: The first prime numbers are 2, 3, 5, 7, 11, 13, 17, 19, 23 and 29.
fact: 2 is the only even prime number, and 1 is not prime.
fact: The Prime Minister leads the government in the UK, Ireland, Canada, Australia and New Zealand.
exercise: Which number is prime? | *7 | 9 | 4 | 15
exercise: «In the UK you do not vote for the prime minister directly.» What is a prime minister in this sentence? | The first coat of paint on wood | *A person who leads the government | A number that only divides by 1 and itself | A very old castle
exercise: What is the only even prime number? | 8 | 4 | *2 | 6
test: Which number is not prime? | 17 | *15 | 13 | 19
test: In «a prime example», what does prime mean? | Wet and muddy | Hot and dry | Very small | *The very best or most important
exam: Which word means to get something ready, like putting a first coat on wood before painting? | Dry | Frame | *Prime | Polish
